//! The `dynamic-range-limit` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! specifies the maximum luminance allowed for High Dynamic Range (HDR) content.
//!
//! Initial: no-limit. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - constrained: Specifies the maximum luminance as somewhat greater than that of HDR reference
//! white, such that a mix of Standard Dynamic Range (SDR) and HDR content can be comfortably viewed
//! together. The precise level is not specified.
//! - no-limit: Specifies the maximum luminance as much greater than that of HDR reference white. The
//! precise level is not specified. This is the initial value.
//! - standard: Specifies the maximum luminance as High Dynamic Range (HDR) reference white, which is
//! the CSS color `white`.
//!
//! Grammar: standard | no-limit | constrained | <dynamic-range-limit-mix()>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-hdr-1/#propdef-dynamic-range-limit
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/dynamic-range-limit
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

